181	      // F17: a code-work legally allowed to outlive the executing leash is reclaimed
182	      // WHILE ALIVE, and the failure is not one duplicate run but a livelock —
183	      // every tenure reclaimed before it can finish, code-work re-executing each
184	      // cycle, the occurrence never converging. The leash is the engine's, so the
185	      // comparison is made where a declaration is judged.
186	      bad(`"code_work_timeout" (${decl.code_work_timeout}s) reaches the executor's ${EXECUTING_LEASH_MS / 60e3}-minute claim leash`,
